ISO-10303-21;
/* Le030: \PE\ selector and \Q\x alternate-quote directive support; ISO 10303-21 Ed.3 §6.4.3 defines \PE\ (UCS extended alphabet-extension) and \Q\x (alternate-quote) directives for use in string literals; legacy generators emit \PE\foo in PRODUCT name fields; alternate-quote directive: \Q\'foo\Q\' encodes a quoted string fragment; parsers that do not implement these directives pass bytes through verbatim producing literal \PE\ or \Q\' in the decoded attribute string; receivers must recognise and consume documented directive operands without lexer desynchronisation; warn-and-accept is the minimum requirement; GEOMETRIC_CURVE_SET IS model entity — OCC yields empty */
